  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:14px">
    <p><span class="chip lore">Index only</span> <strong>Not one image was opened for that table, and
      several names in it are visibly mangled</strong> &mdash; <em>&ldquo;Min Levena Fer&rdquo;</em> is
      FERM&Iacute;N LERENA, <em>&ldquo;Capas-Ra Pelaes&rdquo;</em> is CASIMIRA PELAEZ, and
      <em>&ldquo;Juan Bernardo Serena&rdquo;</em> is the S-for-L this archive has now met five times. It
      is a pointer to plates, not a finding. <strong>And the 1726 artefact is there too:</strong> Lauriana
      Lerena, christened 1891, is indexed with a birth of <em>12 September 1726</em> &mdash; the
      collection&rsquo;s first year standing in for a date it does not have.</p>
  </div>
</section>

